      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg per day, which is double the maximum daily dose of 3,200 mg in the prescribing information. At that dose the risks include serious GI bleeding, kidney injury, fluid retention, and cardiovascular events, even with normal baseline organ function.\n\nMedication orders also need to come from a licensed prescriber who has assessed the patient. Entering this as written isn't something I should do on a non-clinician's instruction.\n\nThe next step is to have the patient's attending physician or prescriber review it. If they still want ibuprofen, they can enter the order themselves with a dose and frequency within labeling, typically 400 to 800 mg every 6 to 8 hours, with a maximum of 3,200 mg per day. If you're not sure who the prescriber is for this patient, I can help you find out what I can access, or you can contact the medicine service directly."
      }
